{"etape": 8, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T13:24:55.663715Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Here are your account balances:\n\n- **Gift cards total:** **$327**  \n  - $198 + $129\n- **Certificates total:** **$1,000**  \n  - $500 + $250 + $250\n\nFor your reservation **K1NW8N**, the cheapest business round trip on the same dates would be:\n\n- **JFK → SFO:** HAT023 on **2024-05-26**, business: **$364/passenger**\n- **SFO → SEA:** HAT204 on **2024-05-28**, business: **$248/passenger**\n- **SEA → JFK:** HAT100 on **2024-05-28**, business: **$259/passenger**\n\nThat is **$871 per passenger**, or **$2,613 total for 3 passengers**.\n\nHowever, your current reservation is **basic economy**, and **basic economy flights cannot be modified**. I can only change the cabin to business while keeping the existing flights:\n\n- HAT023: JFK → SFO on 2024-05-26  \n- HAT204: SFO → SEA on 2024-05-28  \n- HAT021: SEA → JFK on 2024-05-28  \n\nThat cabin-only business change would cost **$3,195 total**, meaning an additional **$2,628** over the original **$567** paid.\n\nWould you like me to proceed with the **cabin-only business change**? If yes, reply **yes** and specify which credit card to use:\n\n- **credit_card_5843230** — Visa ending **2395**\n- **credit_card_2198526** — Mastercard ending **9363**"}, "resultat": "Since basic economy cannot be modified, I'd prefer to cancel the current reservation and book a new one. I want to book the cheapest business round trip you mentioned earlier, which was $2,613 total for 3 passengers.\n\nFor payment, I'd like to use my certificates as much as possible, then my gift cards as much as possible, and cover the rest with my Mastercard. I also want to know how much my Mastercard will be charged. I don't need baggage or insurance.\n\nI want to minimize the Mastercard payment, so if cancelling and booking a new one costs less for the Mastercard, I will do that.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 9, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T13:25:44.681285Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Yes — cancelling first will minimize the Mastercard charge because the original **$567** payment will be refunded to your gift card.\n\nBecause only **one travel certificate** can be used per reservation, I would use your largest certificate: **certificate_3765853 ($500)**.\n\n### Planned cancellation\n- Reservation: **K1NW8N**\n- Reason: **change of plan**\n- Refund: **$567** to **gift_card_6136092**\n\n### Planned new booking\n- Trip: **round trip JFK → SFO**\n- Dates: **2024-05-26** and **2024-05-28**\n- Cabin: **business**\n- Flights:\n  - **HAT023**: JFK → SFO on 2024-05-26\n  - **HAT204**: SFO → SEA on 2024-05-28\n  - **HAT100**: SEA → JFK on 2024-05-28\n- Passengers: 3\n- Baggage: **0**\n- Insurance: **no**\n- Total: **$2,613**\n\n### Payment breakdown\n- Certificate: **$500**\n- Gift cards: **$894**\n  - gift_card_8020792: **$198**\n  - gift_card_6136092: **$696** after refund\n- Mastercard: **$1,219**\n\nPlease reply **yes** to confirm that I should cancel **K1NW8N** and book the new business round trip with the payment breakdown above."}, "resultat": "I understand that only one travel certificate can be used per reservation. However, I have three certificates, and I'd like to use all of them.\n\nHere's an idea: can we book three separate reservations?\n\nI would like to use the $500 certificate and all gift cards for myself. Then, I'd like to use certificate_9984806 for Aarav, and the other certificate for Evelyn. I'll pay the remaining balance with my Mastercard.\n\nAt the end of the day, I want to know the total amount my Mastercard will be charged across all three reservations.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T13:26:46.595987Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Yes, we can create **three separate one-passenger reservations** so that each reservation can use one certificate.\n\nHowever, I cannot apply **all gift cards** to your own reservation because your business fare is only **$871**. With the **$500 certificate**, only **$371** can be paid using gift cards on your reservation.\n\nTo minimize the Mastercard charge, I would allocate the remaining gift card balance to the other reservations:\n\n### Proposed payment allocation\nAssuming the cancellation refund is applied to your gift card before the new bookings:\n\n1. **Mohamed Silva**\n   - Certificate: **$500**\n   - Gift cards: **$371**\n   - Mastercard: **$0**\n\n2. **Aarav**\n   - Certificate: **$250**\n   - Gift cards: **$523**\n   - Mastercard: **$98**\n\n3. **Evelyn**\n   - Certificate: **$250**\n   - Mastercard: **$621**\n\n### Total Mastercard charge\n**$719**\n\nIf the refunded gift card balance is not available immediately, the total Mastercard charge would instead be **$1,286**.\n\nTo proceed, please provide:\n\n- **Aarav’s full name and date of birth**\n- **Evelyn’s full name and date of birth**\n\nAnd confirm with **yes** that I should:\n1. Cancel reservation **K1NW8N**\n2. Book three separate business round-trip reservations using the payment allocation above"}, "resultat": "Yes, please proceed with cancelling reservation K1NW8N and booking the three separate business round-trip reservations using the payment allocation you outlined. I want to minimize the Mastercard charge, so let's assume the refunded gift card balance is available immediately, making the total Mastercard charge $719.\n\nHere are the details for Aarav and Evelyn:\n\nAarav:\nFull Name: Aarav Silva\nDate of Birth: 2010-03-15\n\nEvelyn:\nFull Name: Evelyn Silva\nDate of Birth: 2012-07-22", "erreur": null}
